But it's true that we're more likely to get sick with those conditions when we're under stress as well. What's the difference between good stress and bad stress? I think that bad stress is the kind that makes us distressed or upset. And when those feelings continue over time, that can be particularly detrimental to the body. sometimes stress prepares us to face a challenge. And if we have the resources to meet that challenge, then it can be a positive thing that that sort of incites us to prepare and get ready for things like an important event or a meeting or things like that.

