most comfortable to talk about in the words that people like to use to explain how they're feeling. And in terms of health care seeking, part of its stigma, there's a lot of access issues. Having access to good care and culturally appropriate access to care can be a challenge for many people. So there's a lot of different barriers that could interfere with health thinking, in particular, for ethnically diverse groups. So what would you recommend people do if they think their stress levels are out of control? And, you know, you can talk about this from different groups. I mean, and we're talking about lower income or different ethnic backgrounds or just people who may be more apt to go out and get care.

